Nearly every big open-source project you rely on **started as one or two people deciding** a problem was worth solving. This semester, that's you.

This course is about founding a project rather than joining one: you go find a real need, prove it's real, argue for a solution, build an MVP in the open, and launch it so that others could pick it up and keep building. You lead; others join to build.

